/* ============================================================
   LOGO SIZE — ONE PLACE.
   ROOT CAUSE (found July 28 2026): eye-to-ad-media-logo-denver-seo.png
   contains a large amount of TRANSPARENT PADDING. The artwork occupies
   only a horizontal band in the middle of a much taller canvas. That is
   why height-based sizing shrank the visible mark, and why width-based
   sizing produced a ~330px tall header full of empty space.
   THE FIX: give the img a fixed WIDTH and a fixed HEIGHT window, then
   `object-fit:cover` scales the image to fill the width and crops the
   transparent bands off the top and bottom. Nothing is distorted —
   only empty pixels are cut.
   TO TUNE: `width` controls how big the logo looks. `height` controls
   how much air is around it (raise it if the mark looks cropped, lower
   it if there is dead space). `object-position` is set to 44% rather
   than centre because the artwork sits slightly ABOVE centre in the
   canvas — that is why only the TOP edge was clipping. Change nothing else.
   PERMANENT FIX: crop the padding out of the PNG itself, then this
   collapses to a plain `width` + `height:auto`.
   Breakpoints MUST stay in descending order (largest first).
   ============================================================ */
