        </div>
        <p class="opp-foot">Competitive reads reflect our own work across the Denver metro plus the demographic and growth data cited on this page. They are a starting point for a conversation, not a substitute for looking at your actual market — which is what the free audit does.</p>
      </div>

      <h2 id="industries">The industries that do best in Thornton</h2>

      <p>Three characteristics drive it: young households, high homeownership, and constant new arrivals.</p>

      <h3>Home services</h3>

      <p>The strongest category here, without much competition for the title. Rapid residential growth means roofing, HVAC, plumbing, electrical, landscaping, fencing and remodelling all see sustained demand from homeowners who have never hired one before.</p>

      <p>Worth knowing: construction is the <strong>third largest employment sector among Thornton residents</strong>, with 7,752 people working in it. Your competitors partly live here. So does your labour pool.</p>

      <h3>Healthcare, dental and family services</h3>

      <p>A median age of 34.7 means a lot of young families. Young families need dentists, paediatricians, orthodontists, chiropractors and urgent care — and they need them for the first time, in a city where they may not know anybody to ask.</p>

      <p>Health care and social assistance is the <strong>second largest employment sector</strong> among residents at 9,434 people, so there is both demand and a workforce.</p>

      <h3>Automotive</h3>

      <p>A 31-minute average commute means cars matter. Repair, tyres, auto glass, detailing and collision all perform. The hail exposure across the Front Range adds a seasonal spike on top of the baseline.</p>

      <h3>Retail, dining and personal services</h3>

      <p>Retail trade is the <strong>largest employment sector</strong> among Thornton residents at 9,513 people, and the 120th Avenue corridor is genuinely busy. Restaurants, salons, fitness, childcare and med spas all compete on local search here — often against businesses that have never optimised anything.</p>

      <div class="callout c-tip">
        <p class="c-label">The under-served categories</p>
        <p>The best returns we see in Thornton are usually not in the obvious verticals. Specialist trades, B2B services, niche medical and anything with a longer sales cycle tend to have almost no serious local SEO competition here — because the businesses competing are competing on referrals alone. Those markets can be won in a quarter rather than a year.</p>
      </div>

      <h2 id="included">What a Thornton campaign actually includes</h2>

      <p>Not a list of deliverables for its own sake. This is what has to be true for a business to rank in this city specifically.</p>

      <div class="tbl-wrap">
        <table class="data">
          <caption>The work, why it matters in Thornton, and roughly when it starts producing.</caption>
