          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2 id="timeline">Honest timelines</h2>

      <p>Thornton typically moves faster than Denver proper. Fewer businesses here have invested seriously in local SEO, so the bar to clear is lower. But faster is not instant.</p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Weeks 2–8:</strong> Google Business Profile work begins showing in map results. This is usually the first visible movement and often the first calls.</li>
        <li><strong>Weeks 4–10:</strong> Citation consistency lands. Rankings stabilise where they were previously erratic.</li>
        <li><strong>Months 3–6:</strong> Organic rankings for competitive Thornton service terms start to hold. This is the slow part and there is no way to compress it honestly.</li>
        <li><strong>Months 4–8:</strong> Compounding. Reviews accumulate, content matures, and the map pack position becomes harder for competitors to take back.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>We break the early phase down properly in <a href="/blog/seo-timeline-first-90-days-denver/">what to expect in the first 90 days</a>. The short version is that anyone promising page one in Thornton in thirty days is either talking about a term nobody searches or is not telling you the truth.</p>

      <div class="callout c-note">
        <p class="c-label">Seasonality matters here</p>
        <p>Thornton sits inside the Front Range hail corridor, and demand for roofing, auto glass and restoration spikes hard in a narrow window. Because rankings take three to six months, the work has to start seasons before the money arrives. We mapped the whole calendar in <a href="/blog/denver-seasonal-search-demand/">when Denver customers actually search</a>.</p>
      </div>


      <h2 id="nearby">Thornton businesses rarely serve only Thornton</h2>

      <p>Worth thinking about before you spend anything. Thornton borders Northglenn and Federal Heights to the west and south-west, Westminster to the west, Commerce City to the south-east, Brighton to the north-east, and unincorporated Adams County including Todd Creek to the north. Broomfield sits a short way west across I-25.</p>

      <p>Most Thornton service businesses realistically work across several of those. That is an advantage if you structure it deliberately and a problem if you do not — a service area stretched vaguely across six cities usually ranks properly in none of them.</p>

      <p>The approach that works: <strong>win Thornton first, then expand outward from a position of strength.</strong> A business that genuinely owns its home city has the authority and review base to move into the next one far more cheaply than one starting from scratch everywhere at once.</p>

